; adb_host.loom
; An Apple Desktop Bus (ADB) host: Talk, Listen, Flush and SendReset
; commands and the global reset given by the host on the SPI side; a Talk
; reply of 2 to 8 bytes captured, or no reply reported; a device's Service
; Request (SRQ) seen and reported.
;
; Written on 2026-11-05, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). ADB is in no design document.
; Its one wire is open drain; a bit is a 100 us cell whose low part says
; the value (a 0 is 65 us low then 35 high, a 1 is 35 low then 65 high);
; a command is an 800 us attention low, a 65 us sync high, the command
; byte and a stop bit; the addressed device answers after the stop-to-start
; time Tlt, and any other device may stretch the stop bit's low to 300 us
; to ask for service. The program uses:
;   - an open-drain BIDIR pin (OD_MASK), built for I2C: the host only pulls
;     the line low or lets it go, and the board's pull-up makes the high;
;   - the deadline-latched pin write (SETP ... D, SEMANTICS 6.10), built for
;     clock-exact edges (ws2812): every edge the host makes lands on the
;     clock of its deadline, so each cell's 65/35 split is exact to the clock;
;   - the timed waits (WAITP ... T, SEMANTICS 6.4), built for the receivers'
;     frame timeouts: a device that is missing, early or stuck cannot hang
;     the thread, and "no reply" is the timeout itself;
;   - the tick restart (a write of TICK_INT, SEMANTICS 4), built for UART
;     receivers to lock to a start bit: each received cell's fall restarts
;     the 5 us tick grid, so the sample 50 us later is exact to the clock;
;   - the bit engine's SHI (SEMANTICS 6.9), built for the serial protocols,
;     as a one-bit sampler, MSB first, with CNT counting each 16-bit word.
; What the firmware does that no hardware does: the attention, sync and
; stop bit; the 65/35 coding of each cell; the SRQ test in the stop bit;
; Tlt; the reply's length found from where it stops (8n + 2 cells with the
; start and stop bits) and its framing checked. No hardware in Loom codes a
; bit as the ratio of a cell.
;
; Readings taken on the open spec questions (2026-11-06):
;   - Apple's Guide to the Macintosh Family Hardware was not read; the
;     timings rest on Microchip AN591B, Apple HW01 and TMK adb.c (secondary)
;     and are to be checked against the Guide's table when it is read.
;   - Sync: 65 us sent (TMK); the checker accepts 63 to 72.1 us, which
;     covers AN591's 70 us.
;   - Tlt is the bus-high time from the stop bit's release (or an SRQ's end)
;     to the reply's start bit; the device answers at 200 us.
;   - After an SRQ the addressed device still answers Tlt after it (TMK);
;     a device that stays silent reads as no reply with SRQ set.
;   - A low over 1040 us is a reset at the device.
;   - The bit is read at 50 us after each fall (AN591's receiver): cells of
;     about 77 to 125 us, not the full +-30 %. A low/high ratio decoder
;     would cost about six slots a cell; not done for the word budget.
;   - No random source: the device's address field mixes a host seed with
;     NOW; two Loom devices must be given different seeds.
;
; Pin: AD = BIDIR0, open drain (OD_MASK bit 0). Nothing drives it high.
;
; Host words (FIFO space, thread 0).
;   INQ, one word per transaction:
;     bit 15 = 1: the global reset, the line low for 3 ms (the other bits
;       are ignored);
;     bit 15 = 0: bits 7:0 the command byte, sent as given: AAAA 11 RR Talk
;       register RR of address AAAA, AAAA 10 RR Listen, AAAA 0001 Flush,
;       xxxx 0000 SendReset (AAAA 01 RR and AAAA 0010/0011 are reserved
;       and sent like a Flush: no data phase). For a Listen, bits 9:8 are
;       W - 1, W the number of data words (1..4), and W more words follow
;       in INQ: 2 W bytes, MSB first, the first word's high byte first (an
;       odd Listen length is not offered: the registers a host writes, 2 and
;       3, are two bytes). The program takes them all before the attention,
;       so a Listen never waits for the host on the wire. Bits 14:10 are
;       ignored.
;   OUTQ, per transaction: a status word, then for a Talk reply of N bytes
;   (N + 1) / 2 data words in wire order (an odd N leaves the last byte in
;   the high half and 0 in the low). Status:
;     bits 15:8  the command byte (0 for the global reset);
;     bits 7:4   N, the reply's bytes: 0 for no reply, for a Listen, Flush,
;                SendReset or reset, and for an error;
;     bit 2      the global reset was sent (status 0x0004);
;     bit 1      error: a low that did not end in time (a cell's low past
;                about 90 us, an SRQ past 330 us), a reply whose cell count
;                is not 8 N + 2 with N in 2..8, or a stop bit that is not 0
;                (the start bit is not checked: it is taken as a cell);
;     bit 0      SRQ: the line was still low 10 us after the host let go of
;                the command's stop bit.
;   The PUSHes block while OUTQ is full: the host pops each report before
;   the next transaction (the bus is idle meanwhile, as ADB allows).
;
; Rate: TICK_INT = TK = 5 x US clocks, 5 us at US = 50 (50 MHz). Every ADB
; time is a multiple of 5 us, the coarse tick keeps every WAITD in 8 bits
; (the attention is 160 ticks), and the checker proves the schedule for
; US = 10 as well (the time-scaled build of tools/tests/test_fw_adb.py).
;
; Timing, every figure in us (sources in tools/protomodels/adb.py; Apple's
; Guide to the Macintosh Family Hardware was not at hand and is unchecked):
;     attention   800 low (exact, latched)       AN591 p.2, Fig. 2
;     sync        65 high                        TMK adb.c (800 = 765 + 35)
;     bit cell    100: 0 = 65 low / 35 high, 1 = 35 low / 65 high
;                                                AN591 p.3, Fig. 3
;     stop bit    a 0 bit                        AN591 p.3
;     SRQ         a device holds the stop bit low 300 in all
;                                                Apple HW01; AN591 Fig. 2
;     Tlt         bus high 140..260, 200 nominal, from the stop bit's
;                 release to the data's start bit   HW01; AN591 p.5
;     reset       3000 low                       AN591 p.2; TMK 2.8..5.2 ms
;     reply       start bit 1, 2..8 bytes MSB first, stop bit 0  AN591 p.3
; Receiving. Each cell's fall restarts the tick and the line is sampled
; SAMPLE = 50 us later: a 1's low (35, 24.5..45.5 at the devices' +-30 %,
; AN591 p.2) has ended and a 0's (65, 45.5..84.5) has not; AN591's own
; receiver takes 50 as its threshold (p.5). A low must end by about 90 us,
; and the next fall must come within 90 us of the rise; when it does not,
; the reply has ended and its last cell was the stop bit.
; No reply: no fall within REPLY_TO = 300 us of the bus going high.
;
; OD_MASK (BUGS 14): set first and read back three slots later, as
; dht22_host.loom does and for the same reason (its header): adb_device.loom
; sets its bit with the same three instructions.
;
; Memory: 184 words, 114 in thread 0's quarter (0x000..0x07F) and 70 from
; 0x180 in thread 3's (the end of a reply, the report, the reset and the
; send subroutine), so thread 3 must not be started with this program, as
; the listing says. With adb_device.loom on thread 1 (0x080) and a second
; copy on thread 2 (0x100) the programs load together.
;
; Registers: r0..r3 the data words (a chain: each new word enters at r3 and
; the older ones move down: r0 <= r1 <= r2 <= r3, written out
; where it is used, as a subroutine shared by the timed and the untimed code
; would join their paths for the deadline checker, loomasm README 7), r4 the bit count or a loop count, r5
; the status, r6 TK (the tick restart; a loop count in a Listen), r7 the
; bits being sent and scratch, also the `.csr` scratch.

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 0
        .equ    ADPIN = 0               ; BIDIR0
        .pins   AD = ADPIN
        .equ    ADBIT = 1 << ADPIN      ; its bit in OD_MASK
        .equ    US = 50                 ; clocks per microsecond at 50 MHz
        .equ    TK = 5 * US             ; one tick = 5 us
        .equ    ATT = 160               ; attention, 800 us
        .equ    SYNC = 13               ; sync, 65 us
        .equ    L0 = 13                 ; a 0: 65 us low ...
        .equ    H0 = 7                  ; ... 35 us high
        .equ    L1 = 7                  ; a 1: 35 us low ...
        .equ    H1 = 13                 ; ... 65 us high
        .equ    SRQ_AT = 2              ; the SRQ test, 10 us after the stop's release
        .equ    SRQ_TO = 64             ; an SRQ ends within 320 us more
        .equ    TLT = 40                ; Tlt, 200 us
        .equ    REPLY_TO = 60           ; no fall within 300 us: no reply
        .equ    SAMPLE = 10             ; 50 us after a fall: the bit
        .equ    LOW_TO = 8              ; a low ends by about 90 us
        .equ    HIGH_TO = 18            ; the next fall within 90 us of a rise
        .equ    RST = 200               ; the reset: 3 x 200 ticks, 3 ms
        .equ    DIR = 1 << 1            ; BE_CFG: MSB first, no CRC
        .equ    S_SRQ = 1               ; status bits
        .equ    S_ERR = 2
        .equ    S_RST = 4
        .equ    SPILL = 0x180           ; thread 3's quarter (header, Memory)

; OD_MASK first, read back three slots later (header, BUGS 14).
start:  CSRR    r7, OD_MASK
        ORI     r7, ADBIT
        CSRW    OD_MASK, r7             ; AD open drain
        NOP
        NOP
        CSRR    r7, OD_MASK
        ANDI    r7, ADBIT
        BZ      start                   ; lost to the other thread's write
        .csr    TICK_INT, TK            ; one tick = 5 us; also the checker's .tick
        LDI     r7, 0
        CSRW    TICK_FRAC, r7
        LDI     r7, DIR
        CSRW    BE_CFG, r7
        LDI     r7, ADPIN << 5
        CSRW    BE_PINS, r7             ; SHI samples AD
        LDI     r6, TK
        SETP    AD, 1                   ; released: the pull-up holds it high

; One transaction per host word.
cmd:    POP     r5                      ; blocks
        MOV     r7, r5
        SHLI    r7, 1                   ; C = bit 15
        BC      to_rst
        MOV     r4, r5
        SHRI    r4, 8
        ANDI    r4, 3
        INC     r4                      ; W = bits 9:8 + 1, for a Listen
        SHLI    r5, 8                   ; the status: the command byte in 15:8
        MOV     r7, r5
        SHRI    r7, 10
        ANDI    r7, 3                   ; the command code, bits 3:2
        CMPI    r7, 2
        BNZ     go                      ; not a Listen
        MOV     r6, r4                  ; W, kept for the data phase
        POP     r0                     ; the data words, before the attention
        DEC     r4
        BZ      go
        POP     r1
        DEC     r4
        BZ      go
        POP     r2
        DEC     r4
        BZ      go
        POP     r3

; The command: attention, sync, the byte MSB first, the stop bit.
go:     SETD    0                       ; re-anchor after the unbounded POPs
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   2                       ; the attention's fall
        SETP    AD, 1, D
        WAITD   ATT                     ; 800 us later the sync's rise
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   SYNC                    ; 65 us later the first cell's fall
        MOV     r7, r5                  ; the command byte in bits 15:8
        LDI     r4, 8
        CALL    send                    ; returns at the stop bit's fall
        SETP    AD, 1, D
        WAITD   L0                      ; the stop bit's release
        WAITD   SRQ_AT
        JP      AD, 1, no_srq
        ORI     r5, S_SRQ               ; a device holds the line: SRQ
        SETD    SRQ_TO
        WAITP   AD, 1, T
        BT      to_bad                  ; stuck low
        SETD    SRQ_AT                  ; the bus is high: as without an SRQ
no_srq: MOV     r7, r5
        SHRI    r7, 10
        ANDI    r7, 3                   ; the command code, bits 3:2
        LDI     r4, 0
        CMPI    r7, 3
        BZ      talk
        CMPI    r7, 2
        BNZ     to_rep                  ; Flush, SendReset, reserved: no data

; Listen: Tlt, the start bit, W words from r0 on, the stop bit.
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   TLT - SRQ_AT            ; 200 us after the bus went high
        MOV16   r7, 0x8000
        LDI     r4, 1
        CALL    send                    ; the start bit, a 1
lw:     MOV     r7, r0
        LDI     r4, 16
        CALL    send
        MOV     r0, r1                  ; down
        MOV     r1, r2
        MOV     r2, r3
        DJNZ    r6, lw
        SETP    AD, 1, D
        WAITD   L0                      ; the stop bit, a 0
        LDI     r4, 0
to_rep: JMP     report

; Talk: the reply's start bit within REPLY_TO, then cells until one is
; missing; the last cell received was the stop bit.
talk:   SETD    REPLY_TO
        WAITP   AD, 0, T
        BT      to_rep                  ; no reply (r4 = 0)
        LDI     r7, 17
        CSRW    CNT, r7                 ; the start bit and the first word
rxbit:  CSRW    TICK_INT, r6            ; the fall restarts the tick grid
        SETD    0
        WAITD   SAMPLE
        SHI                             ; the line at 50 us is the bit; Z = word full
        BNZ     rx_n
        STSR    r7
        MOV     r0, r1                  ; down
        MOV     r1, r2
        MOV     r2, r3
        MOV     r3, r7                  ; a whole word into the chain
        LDI     r7, 16
        CSRW    CNT, r7
rx_n:   INC     r4
        SETD    LOW_TO
        WAITP   AD, 1, T
        BT      to_bad                  ; a low too long
        SETD    HIGH_TO
        WAITP   AD, 0, T
        BNT     rxbit                   ; the next cell
        JMP     rx_end
to_bad: JMP     bad
to_rst: JMP     reset

; The rest lives in thread 3's quarter (header, Memory).
        .org    SPILL

; The reply has ended: r4 = 8 N + 2 cells, the last one in SR bit 0.
rx_end: MOV     r6, r4
        SUBI    r6, 2
        MOV     r7, r6
        ANDI    r7, 7
        BNZ     bad                     ; not whole bytes
        SHRI    r6, 3                   ; N
        CMPI    r6, 2
        BNC     bad                     ; under 2 bytes
        CMPI    r6, 9
        BC      bad                     ; over 8
        STSR    r7
        ANDI    r7, 1
        BNZ     bad                     ; the stop bit is not 0
        MOV     r4, r6
        ANDI    r4, 1
        BZ      even
        STSR    r7                      ; an odd N: the last byte and the stop bit
        SHLI    r7, 7                   ; the byte in bits 15:8, 0 below
        MOV     r0, r1                  ; down
        MOV     r1, r2
        MOV     r2, r3
        MOV     r3, r7
even:   MOV     r7, r6
        SHLI    r7, 4
        OR      r5, r5, r7              ; N into status bits 7:4
        MOV     r4, r6
        INC     r4
        SHRI    r4, 1                   ; (N + 1) / 2 words
        JMP     report

bad:    ORI     r5, S_ERR
        LDI     r4, 0

; The report: the status, then r4 words from the chain in wire order (the
; first at r(4 - r4)).
report: LDI     r6, TK
        PUSH    r5
        TEST    r4, r4
        BZ      back
        LDI     r7, 4
        SUB     r7, r7, r4
        BZ      pw
nm:     MOV     r0, r1                  ; down
        MOV     r1, r2
        MOV     r2, r3
        DJNZ    r7, nm
pw:     PUSH    r0
        MOV     r0, r1
        MOV     r1, r2
        MOV     r2, r3
        DJNZ    r4, pw
back:   JMP     cmd

; The global reset: 3 ms low.
reset:  SETD    0
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   2
        WAITD   RST
        WAITD   RST
        SETP    AD, 1, D
        WAITD   RST
        LDI     r5, S_RST
        LDI     r4, 0
        JMP     report

; send: r4 bits of r7, MSB first. Entered with the first cell's fall staged
; or landed at the last deadline; returns with the fall after the last
; cell landed.
send:   SHLI    r7, 1                   ; C = the bit
        SETP    AD, 1, D
        BC      s_one
        WAITD   L0                      ; a 0: the rise 65 us after the fall
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   H0                      ; the next fall 35 us later
        JMP     s_next
s_one:  WAITD   L1                      ; a 1: 35 us
        SETP    AD, 0, D
        WAITD   H1                      ; 65 us
s_next: DJNZ    r4, send
        RET
